1- System Overview & Architecture
  Top-level hardware pipeline
-->Provides a comprehensive overview of the digital video display pipeline designed for the Intel DE10-Lite FPGA .
-System Architecture: Details the top-level integration (vga_top) connecting the clock manager, timing core, block memory, and color multiplexer.
-Clocking & Timing Specs: Explains how the 50 MHz onboard oscillator is synthesized down to a 25.175 MHz pixel clock to meet standard 640 x 480 @ 60 Hz VGA synchronization parameters.
-Dataflow Diagram: Visualizes signal paths from hardware clock pins and switches through internal memory to the board's resistor-ladder Video DAC.

2- Hardware Module Breakdown
RTL and IP core descriptions

-Breaks down every Verilog module and Intel FPGA IP core included in the file
-pll_clock (Intel ALTPLL IP Core): Converts the 50 MHz input clock (PIN_N14) to a stable 25.175 MHz pixel clock to eliminate visual jitter.
-vga_controller.v (VGA Controller Core): Tracks horizontal (0<=h_count<799) and vertical (0<= v_count<=524) scan coordinates, generating hsync, vsync, and active region video_on flags
-vga_top.v (Top-Level Wrapper): Instantiates all components and assigns internal signals to physical DE10-Lite FPGA header pins.

3-Asset Processing Pipeline
-img_to_mif.py Script: Preprocesses standard source images (.jpg/.png) by downsampling them to 320 x 240 resolution using Lanczos filtering.
-Memory Initialization File (canada.mif): Translates 24-bit RGB pixel color values into Altera-formatted hex lines for ROM pre-loading.
-Coordinate Scaling Math: Explains how raster scan addresses are right-shifted (>> 1) to map a $640 \times 480$ grid onto $320 \times 240$ memory bounds.
